### Demo scenario for the IntelliJ HTTP client (or VS Code REST Client).
### Start the service first:  docker compose up -d --wait  &&  ./gradlew run
### Ids carry a timestamp so the file can be run repeatedly against the same database.

@base = http://localhost:8090
@run = {{$timestamp}}

### 1. Capture €121.00 incl. 21% NL VAT -> tax 21.00, fee 6.05 (5% of gross), merchant 93.95
POST {{base}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "paymentId": "pay_{{run}}_1",
  "merchantId": "acme",
  "amount": 12100,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "taxRate": "0.21",
  "taxJurisdiction": "NL"
}

### 2. Same event again (PSP webhook retry) -> 200, nothing posted twice
POST {{base}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "paymentId": "pay_{{run}}_1",
  "merchantId": "acme",
  "amount": 12100,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "taxRate": "0.21",
  "taxJurisdiction": "NL"
}

### 3. Same id, different payload -> 409 idempotency_conflict
POST {{base}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "paymentId": "pay_{{run}}_1",
  "merchantId": "acme",
  "amount": 99900,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "taxRate": "0.21",
  "taxJurisdiction": "NL"
}

### 4. Partial refund of €60.50 -> tax 10.50 back, merchant 50.00 back (fee kept by default)
POST {{base}}/v1/payments/pay_{{run}}_1/refunds
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refundId": "ref_{{run}}_1a",
  "amount": 6050
}

### 5. Too much -> 422 refund_exceeds_refundable
POST {{base}}/v1/payments/pay_{{run}}_1/refunds
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refundId": "ref_{{run}}_1b",
  "amount": 6051
}

### 6. Refund the rest (no amount)
POST {{base}}/v1/payments/pay_{{run}}_1/refunds
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refundId": "ref_{{run}}_1c"
}

### 7. A USD sale in California, another merchant
POST {{base}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "paymentId": "pay_{{run}}_2",
  "merchantId": "globex",
  "amount": 5000,
  "currency": "USD",
  "taxRate": "0.0725",
  "taxJurisdiction": "US-CA"
}

### 8. The payment with its refunds
GET {{base}}/v1/payments/pay_{{run}}_1

### 9. Balances: tax owed per jurisdiction, merchant balances, MoR position, integrity
GET {{base}}/v1/reports/balances

### 10. Balances as of a date (event time)
GET {{base}}/v1/reports/balances?asOf=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z

### 11. Journal for one payment: balanced debit/credit lines
GET {{base}}/v1/journal?paymentId=pay_{{run}}_1
